1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,100
You already know that identity describes
who you are Now

2
00:00:04,100 --> 00:00:08,140
we need to make that knowledge useful
Self-awareness means recognizing

3
00:00:08,140 --> 00:00:12,340
your strengths weaknesses abilities habits
and

4
00:00:12,340 --> 00:00:16,300
the way you usually respond to situations
In the source curriculum

5
00:00:16,680 --> 00:00:20,800
this matters because a person who
understands themselves can make better use

6
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:24,900
of their strengths and work more
deliberately on their weaknesses For a

7
00:00:24,900 --> 00:00:29,060
community leader that is essential
Leadership does not begin with

8
00:00:29,060 --> 00:00:32,960
controlling other people It begins with
understanding what you can

9
00:00:32,960 --> 00:00:37,160
contribute where you still need to grow
and how your behavior affects

10
00:00:37,160 --> 00:00:41,380
the people around you Not every ability
develops in the same way

11
00:00:41,980 --> 00:00:45,980
Some strengths may come naturally to you
while others are built through

12
00:00:45,980 --> 00:00:50,140
effort and practice The important point is
not whether a skill

13
00:00:50,140 --> 00:00:54,200
was given or learned The important point
is whether you

14
00:00:54,200 --> 00:00:58,420
recognize it and develop it At the same
time no

15
00:00:58,420 --> 00:01:02,720
person has every skill a real project
needs One person

16
00:01:02,720 --> 00:01:06,860
may be strong at organizing another at
listening another at

17
00:01:06,860 --> 00:01:09,620
solving problems and another at
communicating

18
00:01:10,920 --> 00:01:15,140
Self-awareness helps you stop pretending
you must do everything yourself

19
00:01:15,140 --> 00:01:19,200
and start understanding where other
people's strengths complete your

20
00:01:19,200 --> 00:01:23,260
own Let's make this personal Complete
these six sentence

21
00:01:23,260 --> 00:01:27,460
starters I can I enjoy I believe

22
00:01:27,460 --> 00:01:31,340
in I spend my time in I am learning to

23
00:01:31,860 --> 00:01:35,900
and I feel when Pause the video and finish

24
00:01:35,900 --> 00:01:39,000
all six honestly either out loud or in
writing

25
00:01:41,020 --> 00:01:45,040
When you come back look at the pattern in
your answers What

26
00:01:45,040 --> 00:01:48,880
do they tell you about your abilities
interests values and habits

27
00:01:49,580 --> 00:01:53,600
This is the real purpose of the activity
not to create perfect

28
00:01:53,600 --> 00:01:57,900
sentences but to help you notice specific
things about yourself that

29
00:01:57,900 --> 00:02:02,000
can shape the way you contribute to a team
and to your community This

30
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:06,080
leads to one of the most important ideas
in the lesson A strong

31
00:02:06,080 --> 00:02:10,180
team is not a group of identical people It
is a group where

32
00:02:10,180 --> 00:02:14,200
different abilities are understood and
combined The source

33
00:02:14,200 --> 00:02:18,060
curriculum makes this clear through
examples such as a school or a

34
00:02:18,060 --> 00:02:22,380
construction project One person cannot
perform every role

35
00:02:22,380 --> 00:02:26,440
alone A project becomes stronger when
people know what they are

36
00:02:26,440 --> 00:02:30,580
good at and trust others with different
responsibilities For

37
00:02:30,580 --> 00:02:34,680
a community leader this means leadership
is not proving that you can

38
00:02:34,680 --> 00:02:38,700
do everything It is helping people use
their different strengths

39
00:02:38,700 --> 00:02:42,880
toward one shared result The rabbit and
turtle example

40
00:02:42,880 --> 00:02:46,980
in the curriculum shows this idea in a
simple way Pause the

41
00:02:46,980 --> 00:02:51,240
video and watch the linked clip As you
watch focus

42
00:02:51,240 --> 00:02:54,780
on the abilities of each character not
only on who wins

43
00:02:55,380 --> 00:02:59,580
Ask yourself what can the rabbit do well
What can the turtle do

44
00:02:59,580 --> 00:03:03,960
well What changes when they understand
their own strengths and weaknesses

45
00:03:04,500 --> 00:03:08,820
And what becomes possible when they
cooperate instead of treating every

46
00:03:08,820 --> 00:03:12,940
situation as a competition When you return
remember

47
00:03:12,940 --> 00:03:17,300
the lesson behind the story Different
abilities are not a problem

48
00:03:17,580 --> 00:03:21,200
They become useful when people understand
how to combine them

49
00:03:22,060 --> 00:03:25,540
Self-awareness also changes the way you
understand other people

50
00:03:26,180 --> 00:03:30,020
Once you begin noticing your own habits
emotions and needs

51
00:03:30,660 --> 00:03:34,720
other people's behavior can become easier
to interpret Someone may

52
00:03:34,720 --> 00:03:38,220
react differently from you because their
priorities personality

53
00:03:38,760 --> 00:03:42,660
or way of working is different That does
not automatically make them

54
00:03:42,660 --> 00:03:47,000
difficult or wrong The source curriculum
connects knowing yourself

55
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:51,120
with being more aware of others because
understanding your own

56
00:03:51,120 --> 00:03:55,600
patterns helps you accept that other
people have patterns too This

57
00:03:55,600 --> 00:03:59,860
is where self-awareness begins to move
outward and become a foundation for

58
00:03:59,860 --> 00:04:04,260
cooperation The bridge video develops this
idea through conflict

59
00:04:04,840 --> 00:04:08,960
Pause the video and watch the linked clip
Notice why the first

60
00:04:08,960 --> 00:04:13,020
characters fail what their selfishness
creates and what the later

61
00:04:13,020 --> 00:04:17,220
characters do differently The lesson is
not that disagreement should

62
00:04:17,220 --> 00:04:21,420
disappear It is that a leader must know
how to manage disagreement

63
00:04:21,420 --> 00:04:25,480
without letting it damage the group A
successful leader listens

64
00:04:26,080 --> 00:04:29,960
understands different points of view and
helps people find a way forward

65
00:04:30,680 --> 00:04:34,960
In a real ACT project team members may
disagree about priorities

66
00:04:35,400 --> 00:04:39,440
roles or solutions Self-awareness helps
you respond to that

67
00:04:39,440 --> 00:04:43,700
conflict instead of simply reacting to it
So what did

68
00:04:43,700 --> 00:04:47,820
you really learn today Self-awareness is
not

69
00:04:47,820 --> 00:04:51,900
just being able to describe yourself It is
knowing how to

70
00:04:51,900 --> 00:04:56,120
use what you understand about yourself You
learned that

71
00:04:56,120 --> 00:05:00,380
strengths should be developed weaknesses
should be worked on or

72
00:05:00,380 --> 00:05:04,500
supported by others different abilities
make teams

73
00:05:04,500 --> 00:05:08,860
stronger and understanding yourself helps
you understand

74
00:05:08,860 --> 00:05:13,580
and work with other people That is why
self-awareness

75
00:05:13,580 --> 00:05:17,820
matters to a community leader Keep your
six sentences

76
00:05:17,820 --> 00:05:21,920
with your personal identity wheel They are
becoming a picture of what

77
00:05:21,920 --> 00:05:26,280
you bring to a team In the next lesson we
move directly

78
00:05:26,280 --> 00:05:30,300
into leadership and explore what
leadership actually means
